    justification: "Investigation shows signatures ALREADY preserve generic type parameters (e.g., Java: '(Map<String, Integer> scores) List<String>', Kotlin: '(items: List<T>, pred: (T) -> Boolean): List<T>', C#: '(Dictionary<string, T> map) List<T>'). Generics are only stripped during type inference for method resolution, which is correct behavior. No work needed."  # 1f3a
